Why do collective groups matter:-

- Governments often use information from [[Think tanks]] and [[Lobbyists]]
    - some members of these have senior government roles as advisors or etc
    - allows rich and powerful to create ideologically driven research and have a loud voice - people who can pay lobbyists or afford lots of research get more of a say
- The BBC allows many non transparently funded think tanks to speak on the news
    - Liz Truss and Kwasi Kwarteng heavily influenced Institute of Economic Affairs - IEA - they have opaque funding so it means we know very little who is paying
    - Means policy will be influenced by research done by biased think tanks with no funding shared
- Revolving doors - politicians work for a few years in parliament and then they go to work in a think tank
    - Ideological issues
    - Connections
- OpenDemocracy - WhoFundsYou
